From 0051ac229422b79cb0eb57061ee85841018bc147 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: 360900 <ziyad.koca@hotmail.com>
Date: Mon, 26 Oct 2026 17:09:23 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] c/gl_client: copy frames through host memory for apps on
 another GPU

An OpenGL app whose context is on another GPU than the runtime, such as
the integrated GPU of a hybrid laptop, can't import the runtime's images;
Mesa crashes in the import of a memory object from another device. The
app's and the runtime's device UUIDs are compared when the client
compositor is created, and when they differ the app draws into plain
textures, which are read back into host memory on release and copied into
the native images by a Vulkan device on the runtime's GPU. Depth images
are not copied, nothing reads them.

The OpenXR state tracker passes the runtime's device UUID to the GL
client compositors for the comparison.
